{"id": "tea:amrtanubhava:1", "source": "src:amrtanubhava", "location": {"ref": "ch.1"}, "paraphrase": "Jñāneśvar salutes the god and goddess, parents of the world, who are one reality appearing as a pair: the god is the being of the goddess and the goddess the manifestation of the god; in their embrace the world arises and their duality itself is lost.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "devotion"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "teachers": ["tch:jnanesvar"], "concepts": ["cpt:siva-sakti-amrtanubhava"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A9"], "notes": "Chapter-level summary.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtanubhava:2", "source": "src:amrtanubhava", "location": {"ref": "ch.2"}, "paraphrase": "Praise of the guru Nivṛtti, whose grace is beyond words and who is the Self shown to itself.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "teachers": ["tch:nivrttinath"], "concepts": ["cpt:guru"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A9"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtanubhava:5", "source": "src:amrtanubhava", "location": {"ref": "ch.5"}, "paraphrase": "The words existence (sat), consciousness (cit) and bliss (ānanda) do not describe the reality: each only excludes its opposite — non-existence, insentience, sorrow — and when the opposites fall away the words fall with them.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "apophatic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "sound-language"], "teachers": ["tch:jnanesvar"], "concepts": ["cpt:cidvilasa"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A9"], "notes": "Chapter attribution recalled; verify.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtanubhava:6", "source": "src:amrtanubhava", "location": {"ref": "ch.6 (refutation of the word)"}, "paraphrase": "The word (śabda), though it removes ignorance and points to the hidden, cannot make the Self known, for the Self is self-evident and needs no proof; scripture's power ends before it.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "apophatic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "sound-language"], "teachers": ["tch:jnanesvar"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A9"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtanubhava:7", "source": "src:amrtanubhava", "location": {"ref": "ch.7 (refutation of ignorance)"}, "paraphrase": "Ignorance cannot exist in the self-luminous reality: if it existed it would be known, and what is known is not ignorance; searched for, it vanishes like darkness searched for with a lamp.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "consciousness-mind"], "teachers": ["tch:jnanesvar"], "concepts": ["cpt:refutation-of-knowledge-and-ignorance"], "terms": ["trm:avidya"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A9"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtanubhava:8", "source": "src:amrtanubhava", "location": {"ref": "ch.8 (refutation of knowledge)"}, "paraphrase": "Knowledge too, as a state opposed to ignorance, dissolves: where there is no ignorance, 'knower' and 'knowing' have nothing to do, and what remains is neither.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "apophatic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["ultimate", "consciousness-mind"], "teachers": ["tch:jnanesvar"], "concepts": ["cpt:refutation-of-knowledge-and-ignorance"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A9"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtanubhava:9", "source": "src:amrtanubhava", "location": {"ref": "ch.9"}, "paraphrase": "The one reality sports as the world without ceasing to be itself — the seen is the seer's own play; so the realized one's life is a natural devotion in which God worships God and every act is worship without a second.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["ultimate", "karma-liberation"], "teachers": ["tch:jnanesvar"], "concepts": ["cpt:cidvilasa", "cpt:bhakti-after-knowledge"], "terms": ["trm:cidvilasa", "trm:sahaja"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A9"], "notes": "'Cidvilāsa' is the later name for this doctrine; the chapter assignment is approximate.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
